WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.080
The headline finding splits in two.

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:03.376
On the positive side,

00:00:03.456 --> 00:00:08.623
the masked-validation-drop search is genuinely
effective at homogeneous selection: it

00:00:08.703 --> 00:00:13.560
correctly identifies the best attention for text
classification and for ListOps,

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:20.658
where Reformer stands out with a drop score of
nearly twelve while every other attention scores below half a point.

00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:21.954
On the negative side,

00:00:22.034 --> 00:00:27.262
when the authors assemble heterogeneous
Transformers that mix several attention types,

00:00:27.342 --> 00:00:32.014
none of them beats the best single-attention model
on any of the three tasks.

00:00:32.094 --> 00:00:36.520
Mixing attention helps you beat the average choice,
but not the best one.
